# experiments/.env — secrets and machine-local endpoints. Nothing else.
#
# experiment.toml owns CONFIGURATION: the ladder, the serving host, the API
# spec, the serving limits, the judge roster, the datasets and the agent
# rosters. `isd-exp freeze write` hashes that file, so a finished run is
# answerable from it.
#
# This file owns what must not be committed, and what is true only of THIS
# machine right now. A value that appears in both is two answers to one
# question and only one of them is fingerprinted, so
# `./isd-exp audit preflight` fails on a duplicate rather than warning.
#
# The launcher does not read DATASET / AGENTS / RUN_TAGS / RATE_LIMIT /
# LADDER_SLOTS from here. It snapshots and restores them around its own
# `source`, so a tuning session cannot redirect an official experiment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Values only; the NAMES are declared in experiment.toml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The bearer token every ladder rung authenticates with.
# The name comes from [serving].key_env. Change it there, not here.
LLM_API_KEY=

# The LLM judge's key. The name comes from [judge].key_env, or from
# [[judge.models]].key_envs when one judge holds several keys that rotate.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Only when [serving].provider = "runpod". Read-only pod listing, used by
# `./isd-exp serve sync-agents` and `sync-embed`; it is not a model key.
# RUNPOD_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local endpoints.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two managed blocks live below this line. Each is delimited by its own
# markers, each is rewritten in place, and neither is edited by hand:
#
#   ./isd-exp serve sync-agents   -> "agent model endpoints"
#     one <SLOT>_AGENT_MODEL_BASE_URLS per rung, plus that rung's NAME and
#     API_KEY_ENVS. Slots are named by [[ladder]].slot.
#
#   ./isd-exp serve sync-embed    -> "embedding endpoints"
#     EMBED_SLOTS, and per served encoder arm <ARM>_EMBED_BASE_URLS,
#     _EMBED_MODEL and _EMBED_API_KEY_ENV. Local and lexical arms need no
#     endpoint and are listed anyway, so the sensitivity sweep runs whatever
#     the endpoint situation is.
#
# With [serving].provider = "static" there is nothing to discover, so the URLs
# are yours to supply: either declare `base_url` on the rung in
# experiment.toml, or set the variable here before running sync-agents. The
# embedding endpoint is always set here first — sync-embed reads
# <ARM>_EMBED_BASE_URLS and writes it back into its block.
#
# NEMOTRON_EMBED_BASE_URLS=https://<host>/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not here any more
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_MODEL_PROVIDER      the client is dispatched on [serving].api_spec;
#                           the vendor label it used to carry is gone
# AGENT_MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW      \
# AGENT_MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS    > [serving] declares all three. They must be
# AGENT_MODEL_STREAMING           /  uniform across every agent and every rung,
#                           which is the fairness argument the comparison rests
#                           on; the launcher writes them onto the benchmark's
#                           command so nothing here can take them back.
# JUDGE_MODEL_*             [judge] + [[judge.models]] declare the roster, and
#                           the launcher passes it as --judge-model-* flags.
#                           Until that section exists, these variables still
#                           answer for the roster and belong in this file.
